Usage:
  x2c translate [options] <input.x>...

Translate each x2c input into a matching C source and header.

Target options:
  -j, --jobs <count>          Maximum parallel translation and compilation jobs

Output options:
      --out-dir <dir>         Write generated files under <dir> (default: .)
      --source-map            Map generated C locations to original x2c sources
      --no-deps               Do not write x2c dependency files
      --dep-file <file>       Override the depfile path (one input only)
      --dep-target <target>   Override the depfile target (one input only)
      --no-phony-deps         Omit phony rules for included files

Source options:
  -I <dir>                    Add a shared x2c/C include directory
      --x-include-dir <dir>   Add an x2c-only include directory
      --package-dir <dir>     Add a directory of x2c packages
      --no-cpp                Skip symbol collection and preprocessing

Inspection options:
      --dump-tokens           Print source tokens and stop
      --dump-ast              Print the parsed AST and stop
      --dump-transforms       Print the transformed AST and stop
      --dump-code             Print unformatted generated code and stop
      --dump-symbols          Print the source symbol table and stop
      --dump-cache            Print the compiler cache and stop
      --dump-conformance      Print protocol conformance and stop
      --dump-symbol-snapshot  Print a complete symbol snapshot and stop
      --dump-header-symbols   Print the header-symbol artifact and stop

General options:
  -h, --help                  Show help and exit
  -v, --verbose               Show commands as they are executed
  -###                        Show commands without executing them
  -q, --quiet                 Suppress successful progress and receipts
      --plain                 Use stable output without terminal rendering
      --color <auto|always|never>
                              Control terminal color
      --debug                 Enable compiler debug logging
  @<file>                     Read additional arguments from a response file
  --                          End option parsing

The output directory defaults to the current directory and must already
exist. Use --out-dir to select another directory.
Shell wildcards are allowed because the shell expands them; x2c does not
interpret wildcard characters in input operands.
